<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Flutter on TECH-ANDGAR</title><link>https://tech-andgar.me/tags/flutter/</link><description>Recent content in Flutter on TECH-ANDGAR</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 07 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://tech-andgar.me/tags/flutter/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>A Comprehensive Guide to Flutter Widget Previews (Beta)</title><link>https://tech-andgar.me/posts/flutter-widget-previews-guide/</link><pubDate>Fri, 07 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tech-andgar.me/posts/flutter-widget-previews-guide/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="overview"&gt;&#10; Overview&#10; &lt;a class="heading-link" href="#overview"&gt;&#10; &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-link" aria-hidden="true" title="Link to heading"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="sr-only"&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Flutter Widget Previews is a powerful experimental feature that allows developers to see widgets render in real-time, separate from a full app, in the Chrome browser. This guide covers how to implement, run, and optimize widget previews in Flutter applications. It is designed to complement the &lt;a href="https://docs.flutter.dev/tools/widget-previewer" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;official Flutter documentation on the Widget Previewer&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="understanding-the-beta-status"&gt;&#10; Understanding the &amp;lsquo;Beta&amp;rsquo; Status&#10; &lt;a class="heading-link" href="#understanding-the-beta-status"&gt;&#10; &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-link" aria-hidden="true" title="Link to heading"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="sr-only"&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;It is crucial to understand what &amp;ldquo;Beta&amp;rdquo; and &amp;ldquo;Experimental&amp;rdquo; mean in a practical sense for your team&amp;rsquo;s workflow.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Missing Dart? When TypeScript Feels Like a Desert</title><link>https://tech-andgar.me/posts/dart-vs-typescript-switch-expressions-collection-control-flow/</link><pubDate>Sat, 11 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tech-andgar.me/posts/dart-vs-typescript-switch-expressions-collection-control-flow/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="missing-dart-when-typescript-feels-like-a-desert"&gt;&#10; Missing Dart? When TypeScript Feels Like a Desert&#10; &lt;a class="heading-link" href="#missing-dart-when-typescript-feels-like-a-desert"&gt;&#10; &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-link" aria-hidden="true" title="Link to heading"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="sr-only"&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;I recently stumbled upon a Twitter conversation that deeply resonated with some of my own &amp;ldquo;pains&amp;rdquo; as a developer. It was about the frustration of working in TypeScript and missing certain syntax features that make life so much sweeter in Dart.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;If you&amp;rsquo;ve ever felt like you were &amp;ldquo;dying of thirst&amp;rdquo; looking for an elegant way to handle conditionals or build lists in TypeScript, you are not alone. Today, we&amp;rsquo;ll explore two of those features that make Dart feel so ergonomic: &lt;strong&gt;Switch Expressions&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;Collection Control Flow&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Solving Artifacts with `ImageFilter.blur` in Flutter on Android, iOS and macOS</title><link>https://tech-andgar.me/posts/solving-artifacts-imagefilter-blur-flutter/</link><pubDate>Sun, 27 Oct 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tech-andgar.me/posts/solving-artifacts-imagefilter-blur-flutter/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="solving-artifacts-with-imagefilterblur-in-flutter-on-android-ios-and-macos"&gt;&#10; Solving Artifacts with &lt;code&gt;ImageFilter.blur&lt;/code&gt; in Flutter on Android, iOS and macOS&#10; &lt;a class="heading-link" href="#solving-artifacts-with-imagefilterblur-in-flutter-on-android-ios-and-macos"&gt;&#10; &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-link" aria-hidden="true" title="Link to heading"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="sr-only"&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/flutter/flutter/issues/157693" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;&lt;img src="https://tech-andgar.me/posts/solving-artifacts-imagefilter-blur-flutter/preview-issue.webp" alt="Flutter ImageFilter.blur Issue"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="introduction"&gt;&#10; Introduction&#10; &lt;a class="heading-link" href="#introduction"&gt;&#10; &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-link" aria-hidden="true" title="Link to heading"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="sr-only"&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;When developing mobile and desktop applications with Flutter, it&amp;rsquo;s common to use blur effects to enhance the user interface. One of the most used methods is &lt;code&gt;ImageFilter.blur&lt;/code&gt;. However, some developers have encountered visual artifacts when applying this effect on Android, iOS and macOS, while it works correctly on web. In this article, we&amp;rsquo;ll explore this issue, understand the reason behind it, and provide an effective solution.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Flutter Test Coverage</title><link>https://tech-andgar.me/posts/flutter-test-coverage/</link><pubDate>Thu, 30 Sep 2021 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tech-andgar.me/posts/flutter-test-coverage/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;LCOV is a graphical tool for GCC coverage testing with gcov. It creates HTML pages containing source code annotated with coverage information by collecting gcov data from multiple source files. LCOV supports &amp;ldquo;Line Coverage&amp;rdquo; and &amp;ldquo;Function Coverage&amp;rdquo; measurement.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The LCOV report looks as follows:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/9597207/79640726-1ad1f680-8161-11ea-9241-d7d6fe70f630.png" alt="image.png"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="installation"&gt;&#10; Installation&#10; &lt;a class="heading-link" href="#installation"&gt;&#10; &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-link" aria-hidden="true" title="Link to heading"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="sr-only"&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="install-on-ubuntu"&gt;&#10; Install on Ubuntu&#10; &lt;a class="heading-link" href="#install-on-ubuntu"&gt;&#10; &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-link" aria-hidden="true" title="Link to heading"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="sr-only"&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;&#10;&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;2&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-shell" data-lang="shell"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;sudo apt-get update -qq -y&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;sudo apt-get install lcov -y&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id="install-on-mac"&gt;&#10; Install on Mac&#10; &lt;a class="heading-link" href="#install-on-mac"&gt;&#10; &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-link" aria-hidden="true" title="Link to heading"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="sr-only"&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;&#10;&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-shell" data-lang="shell"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;brew install lcov&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id="install-on-windows"&gt;&#10; Install on Windows&#10; &lt;a class="heading-link" href="#install-on-windows"&gt;&#10; &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-link" aria-hidden="true" title="Link to heading"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="sr-only"&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Required:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Flutter Interview Questions</title><link>https://tech-andgar.me/posts/flutter-interview-questions/</link><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2020 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tech-andgar.me/posts/flutter-interview-questions/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="flutter-interview-questions"&gt;&#10; Flutter Interview Questions&#10; &lt;a class="heading-link" href="#flutter-interview-questions"&gt;&#10; &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-link" aria-hidden="true" title="Link to heading"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="sr-only"&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#technical-terms-tldr" &gt;Technical Terms TLDR&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#flutter-interview-questions" &gt;Flutter Interview Questions&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#question-categories" &gt;Question Categories&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#questions" &gt;Questions&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#flutter-questions" &gt;Flutter Questions&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#dart-questions" &gt;Dart Questions&lt;/a&